1
00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:03,640
An aerospace panel waits in its fixture.

2
00:00:03,713 --> 00:00:07,800
Engineering has prepared a task change, but the cell needs more than an

3
00:00:07,853 --> 00:00:10,040
instruction sent from somewhere else.

4
00:00:10,173 --> 00:00:14,600
It needs an approved task it can accept, an operator who knows what will

5
00:00:14,669 --> 00:00:17,480
happen, and a result that can be traced.

6
00:00:17,720 --> 00:00:22,600
That is our business question: how do we get from a change that is ready to

7
00:00:22,680 --> 00:00:27,720
work that is accountable? The production floor you see is an illustration.

8
00:00:27,800 --> 00:00:30,680
We have not measured factory delay or savings.

9
00:00:30,707 --> 00:00:35,240
We are building the smallest practical proof of the handoff, before asking a

10
00:00:35,311 --> 00:00:37,160
customer to bet production on it.

11
00:00:37,750 --> 00:00:43,630
Start in engineering. Package one bounded task, identify the receiving

12
00:00:43,710 --> 00:00:47,790
profile, and define the result we expect back.

13
00:00:47,817 --> 00:00:51,790
Think of this as a work package, rather than a remote hand taking over the

14
00:00:51,870 --> 00:00:57,790
robot. In this implementation, the package contains signed joint goals for a

15
00:00:57,854 --> 00:01:01,710
simulator. It carries an exact release identity.

16
00:01:01,843 --> 00:01:06,350
It does not install a driver, a new robot program, or trained weights.

17
00:01:06,530 --> 00:01:10,910
The receiving cell still has its own approval and operating limits.

18
00:01:10,990 --> 00:01:15,870
The exploded view separates those responsibilities: what work is proposed,

19
00:01:15,977 --> 00:01:20,430
where it is allowed to run, and what receipt will connect the outcome to the

20
00:01:20,510 --> 00:01:21,150
request.

21
00:01:21,740 --> 00:01:25,380
Now follow the change across the distance.

22
00:01:25,513 --> 00:01:28,500
An operator chooses the approved capability.

23
00:01:28,600 --> 00:01:33,380
The central dispatcher binds the request to its destination and release.

24
00:01:33,500 --> 00:01:36,180
The delivery channel moves the package.

25
00:01:36,367 --> 00:01:41,380
At the receiving boundary, the local runtime checks what arrived against what

26
00:01:41,428 --> 00:01:43,300
that cell is allowed to accept.

27
00:01:43,460 --> 00:01:46,260
Only an idle executor can activate it.

28
00:01:46,484 --> 00:01:51,140
Once work starts, the task keeps its exact release.

29
00:01:51,284 --> 00:01:56,180
Each boundary answers a business question: did we send the right change, did

30
00:01:56,200 --> 00:01:59,860
the right cell accept it, and can we account for what happened?

31
00:02:00,080 --> 00:02:03,460
The technical checks are available for inspection.

32
00:02:03,600 --> 00:02:09,140
The overarching idea is simple: remote delivery, local responsibility.

33
00:02:09,730 --> 00:02:13,330
This is where the robot earns its place in the story.

34
00:02:13,430 --> 00:02:15,650
The cell has accepted the task.

35
00:02:15,810 --> 00:02:18,850
Local execution now owns the movement.

36
00:02:19,090 --> 00:02:22,970
Cut the central data plane after progress has begun.

37
00:02:23,090 --> 00:02:27,730
In the retained simulator proof, the finite task completes without that

38
00:02:27,780 --> 00:02:33,170
central path. The separate management observer remains available; this is not

39
00:02:33,250 --> 00:02:35,890
a total network blackout or a safety stop.

40
00:02:36,090 --> 00:02:40,290
The robot poses replay committed simulator samples.

41
00:02:40,423 --> 00:02:45,010
To challenge the mechanism yourself, open the workbench and use the real

42
00:02:45,090 --> 00:02:50,210
transfer and disconnect controls. Reconnect and retry the same completed

43
00:02:50,290 --> 00:02:54,850
request: the receipt returns, rather than starting the movement again.

44
00:02:55,440 --> 00:02:59,640
A lost connection and a lost executor are different problems.

45
00:02:59,773 --> 00:03:05,160
If the executor dies, we cannot turn uncertainty into a success message.

46
00:03:05,343 --> 00:03:10,120
Follow the work history. The old task remains visible.

47
00:03:10,236 --> 00:03:13,320
Explicit recovery records it as interrupted.

48
00:03:13,480 --> 00:03:16,360
It does not silently resume the movement.

49
00:03:16,547 --> 00:03:21,880
If the operator decides to try again, that is a deliberately new action, with

50
00:03:21,940 --> 00:03:24,120
its own identity and outcome.

51
00:03:24,328 --> 00:03:29,640
This is the operational value we want to test: can the team understand what

52
00:03:29,702 --> 00:03:34,520
happened, recover deliberately, and avoid accidental repeated work?

53
00:03:34,680 --> 00:03:37,480
The evidence must answer that question.

54
00:03:37,840 --> 00:03:40,960
A polished animation cannot answer it for us.

55
00:03:41,550 --> 00:03:47,330
Now change the task. Inspection positioning and rework positioning already

56
00:03:47,419 --> 00:03:51,410
exercise the same delivery and recovery process in simulation.

57
00:03:51,590 --> 00:03:57,570
The reusable part is the handoff: bind the request, admit the release,

58
00:03:57,640 --> 00:04:02,050
execute locally, retain the receipt, and recover explicitly.

59
00:04:02,180 --> 00:04:07,490
Machine tending and other cell types are possible next modules, shown here as

60
00:04:07,570 --> 00:04:13,090
concepts. Their device interfaces, calibration, tooling and acceptance

61
00:04:13,183 --> 00:04:18,850
still need reviewed adapters. Intel and Red Hat provide the target compute and

62
00:04:18,912 --> 00:04:24,610
platform context. Historical separate-host evidence used Intel processors

63
00:04:24,710 --> 00:04:27,970
and Red Hat Enterprise Linux on OpenShift.

64
00:04:28,066 --> 00:04:33,410
That evidence does not qualify a new host, demonstrate accelerator benefit, or

65
00:04:33,474 --> 00:04:35,850
establish a physical robot installation.

66
00:04:36,440 --> 00:04:41,120
The next commitment is a focused pilot, not a fleet promise.

67
00:04:41,269 --> 00:04:47,200
Choose one bounded task, name the central and edge hosts, and give acceptance

68
00:04:47,253 --> 00:04:52,480
to an owner. Measure the effort from approved release to accepted task, the

69
00:04:52,560 --> 00:04:56,800
manual handoffs, the recovery effort, and the verified result.

70
00:04:57,080 --> 00:05:02,480
Use the dashboard and agent start packet to inspect the implementation and run

71
00:05:02,500 --> 00:05:08,160
the tests. Keep software evidence, compute qualification, and physical cell

72
00:05:08,211 --> 00:05:13,920
acceptance distinct. Red, amber and green must refer to a specific

73
00:05:14,032 --> 00:05:15,360
test and its scope.

74
00:05:16,100 --> 00:05:21,972
From change to work: deliver the capability, keep control local, and

75
00:05:22,052 --> 00:05:24,212
earn the next step with evidence.
